Package: soviclust
Type: Package
Title: An Interactive R Package for Social Vulnerability Assessment, Spatial Diagnostics, and Fuzzy Geodemographic Clustering
Version: 0.7.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      given = "Deden",
      family = "Istiawan",
      email = "dedenistiawan@gmail.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")
    )
  )
Description: Provides an interactive Shiny workflow for social vulnerability
    assessment, spatial diagnostics, and geodemographic clustering. The package
    implements a principal component analysis (PCA)-based Social Vulnerability
    Index (SoVI) workflow inspired by Cutter, Boruff, and Shirley (2003)
    <doi:10.1111/1540-6237.8402002>, including alternative indicator-direction
    strategies, proportional PCA-based weighting, Jenks classification, Global
    Moran's I, and Local Indicators of Spatial Association (LISA). Clustering
    methods include K-Means, Fuzzy C-Means (FCM), DBSCAN, ClustGeo, Fuzzy
    Geographically Weighted Clustering (FGWC), Local Fuzzy Geographically
    Weighted Clustering (LFGWC), and Adaptive Local Fuzzy Geographically
    Weighted Clustering (ALFGWC). The FGWC-related implementation is adapted
    from the GPL-3-licensed 'naspaclust' framework. 'soviclust' extends the
    optimization options with Grey Wolf Optimizer (GWO) and Whale Optimization
    Algorithm (WOA), and implements ALFGWC with adaptive neighborhood influence
    based on Local Moran's I and selectable distance-threshold, Queen, Rook, and
    Bishop neighborhood structures. The application also provides fuzzy cluster
    validation, repeated-run stability assessment, interactive mapping,
    diagnostic visualization, and result export.
